  "cache_write is the price of tokens written to the prompt cache. Anthropic: the 5-minute write price (the 1-hour write costs more and is not used). OpenAI: the page lists a cache-write price for the gpt-6 and gpt-5.6 families; input tokens are Input, Cached Input or Cache Write, never more than one. Omitted where the page shows none (OpenAI gpt-5.5, gpt-5.4 and older, and Gemini): such tokens bill as input, so Cost() prices them at the input price.",
  "long is the price of a request whose whole prompt (fresh input, cache reads and cache writes) is over long.over tokens: Anthropic Haiku 5.5 over 100000; OpenAI over 272000 (the page says short context is up to and including 272K); Gemini 3.1 Pro and 2.5 Pro over 200000.",
  "valid_until: the last day (UTC) the price is valid; the provider announced a change after it, so later requests have an unknown cost.",
  "Gemini audio input costs more than text; this app sends text and images only, so the text price is used."
